592	    case "damageChosen": {
593	      // The snipe (Hawlucha / Meowscarada): choose `count` of the opponent's
594	      // Benched Pokémon and put counters on each. An empty Bench is a no-op.
595	      // The pick asks for `count` EXACTLY — the printed number is a floor as
596	      // well as a ceiling (effects.ts) — clamped to the Bench by §8.6 "do as
597	      // much as you can", which is the only thing that softens it.
598	      //
599	      // WHAT DECIDES BETWEEN A PROMPT AND AN AUTO-TAKE IS `optional`, NOT THE
600	      // BENCH SIZE. A mandatory snipe over a Bench of `count` or fewer has no
601	      // decision left in it, so it auto-takes (the M1 no-choice doctrine, and
602	      // the parkOrForce family's rule at one candidate). A DECLINABLE one always
603	      // has a decision left — "you may" — and it is the same decision on a Bench
604	      // of 1 as on a Bench of 5, so it parks at every non-empty Bench. Auto-
605	      // taking there would honour Hawlucha's printed "you may" only when the
606	      // opponent has more than 2 Benched Pokémon, which is not what the card
