20	// 0.38.0 → 0.39.0 — the ANY-target snipe family.
21	//
22	// "This attack does N damage to 1 of your opponent's Pokémon. (Don't apply Weakness
23	// and Resistance for Benched Pokémon.)" is the WHOLE attack (no `damage` field) — a
24	// chosen hit on the Active OR a Bench. `damageChosen` gained `target: "opponentAny"`
25	// (candidates = the opponent's Active + Bench); `placeSnipe` an Active arm that runs
26	// the §8.5 W/R pipeline, because Weakness/Resistance apply ONLY to the Active — a
27	// Benched pick stays flat. Rotom sv01-069 "Linear Attack" (Lightning, 20) is the W/R
28	// witness: 40 on a {L}-weak ACTIVE, 20 on the SAME body Benched. Fezandipiti ex
29	// sv06.5-038 "Cruel Arrow" (Darkness, 100) is the big flat twin.
30	//
31	// 0.46.0 — the ignoreWR rider (Umbreon "Feint Attack" sv03-130): a second sentence,
32	// "This attack's damage isn't affected by Weakness or Resistance, or by any effects
33	// on that Pokémon.", sets `damageChosen.ignoreWR`, which nulls the target's W/R AND
34	// its reduction passive on both arms while keeping the attacker's own pre-W/R bonus.
35	// fix-feint (a synthetic {L} witness carrying the verbatim SV text) is the tester: on
36	// the {L}-weak Active the 50 stays FLAT (not doubled), and a benched Bouffalant's −20
37	// Bouffer is skipped.
